{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3115","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3115","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3115\",\"parent_revision\":\"5aa670205c1caa6c45e6c506ab9136e44d1cb8a70128b7a1a65870e4ea7203eb\",\"root_revision\":\"5aa670205c1caa6c45e6c506ab9136e44d1cb8a70128b7a1a65870e4ea7203eb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAgent roles in the development-harness are currently inferred from the voice of whatever prose an agent is handed, rather than assigned as data. In the #3060 incident a task-worker handed orchestrator-voiced skill text inferred a coordinating role and began dispatching its own teams and worktrees, costing ~$100 of unplanned spend. Four prose changes encode the role vocabulary so the role is stated, never inferred.\\n\\nScope (all four, one vocabulary decision expressed in four places):\\n\\n1. plugins/development-harness/CONTEXT.md \u2014 add the role terms as glossary definitions only (CONTEXT.md is a glossary, never a spec): orchestrator = the single interactive agent acting on behalf of the human; manager and worker = agents acting on behalf of their dispatcher; the manager role exists only by explicit assignment from the dispatcher and is never self-inferred; role is carried as data (dispatch prompt or plan metadata) and is never detected by harness introspection, because the plugin targets Claude Code, Codex and OpenCode and system-prompt introspection is Claude-Code-specific.\\n\\n2. plugins/development-harness/docs/adrs/ \u2014 a new ADR recording the decision and its reasoning (the reasoning belongs here, not in the glossary). Follow the existing filename convention, cf. ADR-1770-1-single-writer-task-backend.md. Cover: the alternative of harness runtime introspection and why it was rejected (not cross-harness portable), and that sub-dispatch itself is legitimate when planned \u2014 the defect is exclusively role self-assignment.\\n\\n3. plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md \u2014 rewrite the Identity section from open-ended framing (currently 'You become whatever the task requires') into a closed enumeration of the jobs a worker performs: read the task, profile_load, start-task, report, stop. State explicitly that the worker never dispatches other agents unless its own dispatch prompt explicitly assigns it the manager role.\\n\\n4. plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/post-planning.md \u2014 add a one-line warning that the dh:implement-feature invocation runs inline in the current agent's context and must never be copied into a delegation prompt.\\n\\nConstraint: plugin content is a standalone distributed product \u2014 no references to .claude/rules/ or to this repository from inside plugins/**.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **encode orchestrator/manager/worker role vocabulary in dh plugin prose** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"39fd38ebaa5c21724fac44b31bb60fe4d1ae9a9f6d2e84f81b3a328e3c2fa78f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQIophw\"}"}